cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If ngsrng helps your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ngsrng: random functions on finite element spaces"
abstract: >-
  ngsrng samples random functions (Gaussian, log-normal, uniform, gamma, Student-t, Wishart and other random
  fields) in NGSolve finite element spaces, with numpy's sampling API, on CPU and GPU. It includes exact Matérn
  priors, posteriors of Bayesian inverse problems, variance maps and trace estimators.
authors:
  - family-names: Aarset
    given-names: Christian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8163-9305"
version: 0.0.1
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/CAarset/ngsrng"
url: "https://github.com/CAarset/ngsrng"
keywords:
  - random fields
  - Gaussian random fields
  - finite element method
  - NGSolve
  - Matérn
  - SPDE
  - uncertainty quantification
  - Bayesian inverse problems
  - PyTorch
